{"term":"flatter","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:5d99af3b091e5f7311","definition":"comparative form of flat: more flat","example":"","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"comparative, form-of","register":"comparative, form-of","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flatter#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0f92995f4c2169602f","definition":"To compliment someone, often (but not necessarily) insincerely and sometimes to win favour.","example":"A man that flattereth his neighbour spreadeth a net for his feet.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["butter up","lay it on thick","puff"],"antonyms":["defame","offend"],"collocations":[],"usage":"ambitransitive","register":"ambitransitive","wordFamily":["beflatter","flatterable","flatteress","flatterize","flatter oneself","flatterous","flattersome","flatter to deceive","outflatter","overflatter","unflatter"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flatter#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8cccf0c561cf02e12a","definition":"To enhance or gratify someone's vanity by praising them.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":["stroke someone's ego"],"antonyms":["defame","offend"],"collocations":[],"usage":"ambitransitive","register":"ambitransitive","wordFamily":["beflatter","flatterable","flatteress","flatterize","flatter oneself","flatterous","flattersome","flatter to deceive","outflatter","overflatter","unflatter"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flatter#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6dc28f00a9586345e3","definition":"To portray someone to advantage.","example":"Her portrait flatters her.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["brush up to","collogue","flatter","flatterize","gl